WEBVTT

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.280
They say food is a good recovery gift.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.120
You eat it and then it's gone,
so it symbolizes the illness leaving.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.490
I hear bath salts are nice too.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.120
They mean all the sickness is washed away.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.790
Bath stuff, huh? That could be good!

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.860
Are you guys dumb or what?

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.070
"Recovery gifts" are supposed to be
<i>from</i> the recovered person, not <i>to</i> her.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.740
You came.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.140
She is a classmate, after all.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:34.740
Now, now. She invited us to a party,
so we should bring gifts.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.310
Right, Ryo?

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.850
Hey, isn't Senkawa late?

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.480
Dang it, he's always like this!

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.420
What are you looking for here, Birdy?

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.410
Just come on.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.860
It's Hayamiya.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.330
Leave it for later.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.430
Hey! What was that for?!

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.030
I promised to go to
Nakasugi's house today, you know!

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.600
You're my Buddy, aren't you?

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.540
W-Well, yeah, but...

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.870
Don't worry, we'll be done soon.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.270
Are you sure?

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.270
Trust your Buddy!

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.290
Which one should I wear?

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.700
I guess this one really is no good...

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.130
What should I do?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:17.210
Is this really the place?

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.680
Yeah, Kitamura and I have been here once before.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.180
She said it was a "normal house"...

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.720
What's normal about it?!

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.550
What are you flipping out about?

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:30.990
Nakasugi's the same person
no matter what house she lives in!

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.220
Yes?

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:39.360
U-Um, I'm the e-esteemed Miss Sayaka
Nakasugi's h-humble schoolmate...

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.530
What are you flipping out about?

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.520
Hi, I'm Kitamura, Miss Nakasugi's classmate.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.240
We've been expecting you.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.070
Oh, brother...

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.500
It's amazing inside, too...

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:00.050
It's like a movie set.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.450
Hello, everyone!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.390
Nakasugi...

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.190
Whoa, cute...

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.360
You look cute, Nakasugi!

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:13.200
Thank you! I bought this for today's party.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.530
That color looks great on you.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.940
Thanks. Um, where's Senkawa?

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:23.570
O-Oh, him. The jerk's
disappeared off somewhere again.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.710
He's not even answering his phone.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.110
Oh...

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.810
Ah, that's right. Here, Nakasugi.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:36.450
This is a little present from us.
Congrats again on getting well.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:42.880
We've caused you all worry,
but as you can see, Sayaka is fine now.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:49.470
I'm afraid I have to leave early,
but I hope you'll enjoy yourselves.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.900
Here we go!

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:01.080
This is baked king crab wrapped in sole

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.910
and champagne sauce flavored with beets.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:07.750
Huh? Crab and beef what?

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.090
Yoshie, I'd like some <i>viande,</i> too.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.360
Miss?

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.630
She used to be so sickly,

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.100
but now it seems she's healthier
than before she was hospitalized!

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.260
Yes, talk about luck!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.670
Hey, that was rude!

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:28.660
Well, it's true, isn't it?!
Her side of the car was crushed!

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.680
But by the time we visited her the next day...

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:39.220
She escaped with nothing but a light concussion.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:42.550
- Truly, it was a miracle.
- Grandfather!

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:44.890
Let's stop talking about the accident.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:51.130
I don't want to remember it.
I'll have bad dreams...

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:55.830
Sheesh, you and your big mouth!
You have no delicacy!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.130
Well, excuse me!

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.870
I know, why don't we go out into the courtyard?

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.000
Huh?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.170
French-style eating is a little too formal, isn't it?

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.210
Yoshie, let's have a buffet-style meal instead.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.210
Oh, that sounds good!

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.640
I'm in!

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:14.310
<i>Medically, this is inexplicable.</i>

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.260
<i>She's fully recovered from all</i>
<i>the damage to her lungs and brain.</i>

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:22.590
<i>I've never seen a case like this.</i>

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:26.500
<i>The only possibility is that the damaged</i>
<i>tissue spontaneously regenerated.</i>

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:28.490
<i>It's an unbelievable phenomenon.</i>

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.400
This is weird...

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.870
What are you doing?

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.370
Tracking down where the marionettes came from.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.840
Marionettes?

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.240
What you call "robots" here.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.510
Robots here in an abandoned hotel?

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:46.050
Yep.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:50.220
Was it a problem for me to visit
you just as you were going out?

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.190
Nonsense, of course not.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:54.920
This way I can get rid of a certain
nuisance while I drop you off.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.190
So, what did you come to find out today?

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:01.600
I hear you're meeting
frequently with someone lately.

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:08.070
You know, they say "He who
chases two hares catches neither."

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.140
Are you on your way to see him now?

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:16.910
This is a business trip. Unlike you,
<i>I have lots of work I need to do.</i>

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:16.980
"G&G Company"
This is a business trip. Unlike you,
<i>I have lots of work I need to do.</i>

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:19.900
"G&G Company"

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:25.390
I'll warn you about one <i>thing:</i>

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:30.230
the Altan investigator is trying
to dig up dirt on the Ryunka.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:34.900
Growing the Ryunka is a whole
different world from making a marionette.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.470
If you're not careful, you'll get yourself hurt.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:41.240
Don't assume you have much time.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.070
An alien, eh?

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.170
I'll be fine.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:51.170
If worst comes to worst...
that's why you let me have her, right?

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.750
This is tasty!

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.520
Hey, Nakasugi, what's this called, again?

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:06.760
Hmm? I think it's <i>"Veau Poêlé."</i>
I would guess the sauce is Marsala wine.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:09.500
<i>Veau Poêlé</i> with Marsala wine sauce!

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.270
Can you say that, Chigira? Try it!

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:15.200
<i>V- Veau Poêlé</i> with Marks...

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.200
Nope, you messed up!

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:22.880
The buffet was a good call. I gotta
tell you, it was rough at the table.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:27.320
I'm sorry. My grandfather
was trying to be thoughtful.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.890
So what does he do for a living?

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:30.790
Huh?

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.490
His company makes high-tech
machines and stuff, right?

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:37.860
He has tons of amazing engineers, huh?
I saw them on TV.

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:41.860
He's donated to our school, too, right?

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:45.800
People call him by a lot of titles.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.310
But to me, he's my only relative,

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:54.910
who raised me in place of my dead parents.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:57.050
We have to walk on eggshells with this girl.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.850
Don't say stuff like that!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.250
Say!

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.680
Why don't we all go for a swim?

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.750
Miss!

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:15.530
Oh, so that's why you told
us to bring our swimsuits!

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:19.240
I've been looking forward to this!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:22.440
Hayamiya, can you call Senkawa again?

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.870
S-Sure.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.600
Jeez... I'll text him again.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:38.350
Hey!

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:39.420
What?

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.690
You <i>know</i> what! The party started a long time ago!

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:46.090
You saw the Tragedy of Bilugeva too, didn't you?

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:59.810
Ryunka is "invisible death"
in the ancient Empire language.

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:03.450
We have to find it, fast.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:07.750
And even if Geega was the
one who brought it to Earth,

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.920
he must've had an accomplice here, right?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.320
We're going to find out who.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.730
Birdy, can you switch with me?

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:49.250
Shit!

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.030
Geega!

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.480
I died, didn't I?

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:33.870
Pinup girls going missing?

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:36.010
Oh, I remember that!

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:41.080
All the girls who disappeared had
something to do with Giga's show.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:43.210
He was a producer at your station.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:46.820
I was wondering what made
you call me up out of the blue...

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:49.320
They say Mr. Giga was fired.

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:52.020
I've never met him, so I wouldn't know much...

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:56.590
And? What story are you <i>really</i> working on?

00:11:56.590 --> 00:12:00.160
The pinup girls scoop is
way past its expiration date.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:03.900
I can't believe you'd stick with it for long.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.530
What are you really after?

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:12.240
Your wallet. I thought I'd have
Empire TV's star newscaster buy me lunch.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:16.180
I saw your interview with Satyajit Shyamalan.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:19.350
I didn't go on that show for the fun of it.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:22.080
And he was the one who
offered to do the interview.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:26.760
What's a TV station doing toadying
up to the CEO of one business?

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:30.190
Shyamalan's Playmaker Industrial Company

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:34.300
did all the planning and
production for our hit show.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:37.370
He gets us the numbers. We can't go against him.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:41.240
If we offend him, he'll leave
us for someone else in no time.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:44.870
Basically, the station doesn't
want to wreck the honeymoon.

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:48.210
"Thank the gods for Shyamalan,
the King of the Media," eh?

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:49.950
That's the size of it.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:53.880
Seems like there's no one left
at the station who can defy him.

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:58.090
So even the press, that force for justice,
is a slave to the numbers.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.790
What a sad reality!

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:04.060
Did you call me all the way out
here so you could be sarcastic?

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:10.270
Did this Giga guy get hired on
Shyamalan's say-so, by any chance?

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:13.000
Wow, I'm impressed you knew that.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.600
I had a hunch...

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:20.140
Oh, I have to get to the studio,
so I'll be going now.

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:21.510
See you later, Mr. Muroto.

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:22.940
Sure.

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:28.250
Reality is harsh, huh Sanada?

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:29.650
Here it comes!

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:32.920
Right!

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:33.910
Here!

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:41.130
Cut it out, Sudou!

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:43.200
You did that on purpose!

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.930
Dunno what you're talking about!

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:45.920
Sheesh!

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.350
Here.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:14:00.180
Thanks. Hey, Nakasugi, are you okay?

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:03.350
I'm fine. I'm just a little tired, that's all.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:05.980
I'll join you after I've rested a little more.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:10.360
Here I go!

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:11.560
Got it.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:12.990
Nice catch!

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.170
Is Nakasugi okay?

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:21.640
She looks like she wants to swim.
Let's wait and see.

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.870
I'm a little surprised, though.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:25.010
Hmm?

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:30.980
She always used to be more reserved,
or more like gloomy, you know?

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:36.350
Yeah, she does seem kinda different,
wearing that flashy dress and all...

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:41.160
And come to think of it, it's like
she's been obsessing over Senkawa...

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.820
Wait, you don't think...

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:43.330
Huh?

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:46.030
What? No way! Not Senkawa!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.330
But she was totally acting that way!

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.930
Hey, no having a private party over there!

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:52.230
Quit chatting and start swimming!

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:53.220
Shut up!

00:14:56.070 --> 00:15:00.880
I was quite surprised when
you said you would swim, Miss,

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:06.250
but I see now you were doing
it to let your friends have fun.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.680
That's not it.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:09.080
What?

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:15.120
I really do feel sick. I need to rest a little...

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.230
Here it comes!

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:17.090
Right!

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:18.080
One more time!

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:29.470
I've been expecting you, Satyajit Shyamalan.

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:34.040
Thank you for coming all this way.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:39.040
No, I apologize for
inconveniencing you, Mr. Nakasugi.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:03.390
Miss...

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.350
Senkawa!

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:15.520
I was afraid you wouldn't come.

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:19.290
I'm sorry. A lot of stuff happened...

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:21.920
I guess Hayamiya and the others
were probably pissed, huh?

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.910
You might be in for it tomorrow.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:36.200
So, um... How are you feeling? Are you all better?

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.210
Yes. I'm just fine now.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:41.510
Yoshie says I shouldn't push
myself too hard yet, though.

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:43.180
Yoshie?

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.810
That woman there.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:49.180
She's lived and worked here since I was little.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:53.790
But... maybe she's right.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:57.190
I get so groggy sometimes.

00:16:57.190 --> 00:16:59.800
And I can't remember anything...

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:04.730
Sometimes I'll start a book I've
already read again from the beginning.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:08.200
You know what? I died.

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:13.410
I died in that accident.
And everyone else did, too...

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.880
But now I'm alive even though they're not...

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:20.020
God gave me a new life. I'm a new me.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:23.420
I'm sure I was reborn.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:24.850
I get that.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:30.190
I wanted to thank you.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:35.000
You're the one who carried me
to the nurse's office that day, right?

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.430
Huh?

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:40.000
A scary man grabbed me on the roof,

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:42.400
but then when I woke up
I was in the nurse's office...

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:50.010
Er, well, that was... um...

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:52.710
Thank you, Senkawa.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.550
N-Nakasugi?

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:58.710
Um, l...

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:03.060
Senkawa?!

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.050
Miss!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.570
Achoo!

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:32.790
You should've stayed until your
clothes dried, like they told you to.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.590
They're dry now.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:37.130
Anyway, you two had a nice mood going there.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:40.830
Sayaka Nakasugi's a pretty assertive girl.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:43.230
I can see why you'd get a hormone rush.

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:45.930
I told you, stop saying "hormone rush"!

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.140
I mean, it's not like that...

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.570
- I mean, she's too...
- What's that? I can't hear you!

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:55.340
Was I right about buying the flowers, or what?

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:57.280
You ought to thank me!

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.250
Says the girl who made me late in the first place.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:03.150
But that was an impressive idea, coming from you.

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:08.960
Shion Arita's gotten lots
of flower bouquets, yessiree!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:12.360
They're pretty nice to get.
It's a good Earth tradition.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:55.300
That is not the Miss Sayaka I know!

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.840
She used to be so quiet,
and she always wanted to be alone,

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:00.980
but she was so lively with her friends today!

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:02.580
What a strange thing to say.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:07.380
Sayaka becoming more cheerful
is the best thing we could ask for!

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:11.350
And her clothes? What about those clothes?

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:17.660
